00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.300
It's another football game on the NES.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.880
I mean, you say that as if there's been a dozen.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.600
There's only been like two, three so far, right?

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.020
What are the three? What are the three in your mind?

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.680
I want you to list off everyone that you can remember because this will be interesting.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.960
Okay. So obviously there's Tecmo Bowl.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.000
Correct. The only essential one.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.740
Which I think we all like that.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.340
We've got 10-yard fight, our first episode ever.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.380
Hell yeah. And then one of them was named after a quarterback.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.020
John Elway. Yeah.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.240
Okay. It was John Elway.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.320
John Elway's quarterback club or something like that.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.400
I think that was right.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.220
Yeah. And there's one more.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.580
There was one more.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.860
Yes. It's very obvious, but I don't expect you to get it.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.580
Wow. That's kind of insulting.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.240
But tell me, Mike.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.400
I believe it was just called NFL or National Football League.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.780
Oh, I think you're right.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:46.720
And I don't remember a, I can't conjure a single image in my head of what that looked like.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.080
I know it was very disappointing.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.420
Yeah. It's called NFL football.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.260
So National Football League football.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.520
And the weird one about that one was that it was developed by Atlas, the people who make Persona now.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:05.760
But NFL football was cool because that had the NFL license.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.820
So you could play as the team.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.120
They only had like 12 of the teams though, right?

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.080
I don't remember that part.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:19.840
But I do remember that that didn't matter because you don't want to be the Buffalo Bills if the game sucks.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.080
Yeah. I mean, that's true.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:37.160
The problem here, of course, with NES Play Action Football, a game made by Nintendo, released for the NES, is that they didn't get the NFL license, but they also just didn't seem to care.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:47.000
Did you notice that like the teams are, even though they're not calling them the Los Angeles Rams, they are the same, like the players' names?

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.440
Yeah, they got the license from the NFL Players Association.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.920
Yeah, but also like, and then they're matching them to the teams from the cities they were in.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:55.940
For sure, for sure.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.380
So like, Marino's on the Dolphins, Montana's in the game.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.180
It's like, you know, it's like, they got the right people.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.100
So it's basically like, just squint hard enough and you are playing an NFL game.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.620
I agree.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:20.140
And I think at this point, when it's really hard to even put a logo on a screen with like the amount of pixels that you have, I think that just the NFL PA license is enough.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:38.620
And it's like, I'd say that if you had to choose between having the teams and having the players, I think the players in the league are more important than, or at least more like, you can connect with them more than like the league itself.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:46.000
At least in my opinion, at this point in our journey of simulation.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:55.040
And how many players need to be in the game for it to like, for it to feel real to you?

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:05.160
Like if it was just, you know, Josh Allen's NFL football, and he was the only real NFL player because it's his game and everybody else is just made up.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.880
Can you, can you get into that?

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.480
I think that that's a ridiculous thing.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:18.620
And I, but I also don't think it's too far away from how they did it here because they only did like eight teams, which I don't truly understand.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:28.760
Like why they're only doing, it's like, it's like New York, Miami, Denver, LA.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.640
It's like some, yeah, Chicago.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:38.040
Like these are like the big market teams for the most part, but I don't really, I just don't know why they did it that way.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:45.420
Like if you're going to get the license for the whole union and have, you'll, you have access to every big name.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.860
You're only going to have a, a quarter of the league in it.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.700
Not sure why. Yeah.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:57.500
It's 1990 and you choose the New York giants over the Buffalo bills.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.380
Well, this is 1990.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:02.020
So we haven't even been, you know?

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.460
Okay. So it's, it's just coming pretty soon.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:10.320
The Buffalo bills, like the ones that we want to play where they're going to be the best team in the league.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:11.220
The team's there.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.880
It's just, uh, it, you know, there's still the bickering bills right now.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.980
Right. The stats aren't adjusted for them being the best.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.500
It's true. You know, it's like really upsetting when every version of MLB, the show comes out.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:30.600
And it's like, if the Mets had an, had an okay year, the same players that were in the, you know, run the previous year now have like weaker stats.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:33.500
It's like, they're the same players, but they're older now.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:38.700
I don't know. We're older now too, since 10 yard fight.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:45.580
We are. And that's what I kind of wanted to talk about because I'm not trying to be mean to this game.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:56.680
This game is not 10 yard fight, but is it really like we're talking now five years later after 10 yard fight, obviously much longer in the podcast time, but five years between 1985 and 1990.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.240
And I don't think that this is feeling all that different from 10 yard fight.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.940
Well, okay. Let's, let's talk about like the most obvious difference here.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.460
And that's just the perspective.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.880
Yeah. And that's what we're, that's what we're going to focus on.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:12.820
I feel like a lot, right.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.700
Do you want to, do you want to talk about what the perspective changes?

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:26.680
Yeah. It's, it's one of, it's just one of those decisions that you kind of have to wonder like, wow, this sounded a lot better in the pitch meeting than it did in execution.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:32.080
Um, so we've seen vertical football in 10 yard fight.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:39.920
We've seen horizontal football in Tecmo bowl, at least in terms of like, what is the orientation of the field on the screen?

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:56.660
Mm-hmm. And both of them have their pros and cons, but at no point did I think that moving everything 45 degrees for like this faux 3D effect on this system would make things feel better.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.780
It's better. It's obvious.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.940
It's definitely a striking image.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.000
Right. And it's just 45 degrees.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:04.480
It's not even really like isometric.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:12.740
Like I don't get any sense of 3D depth out of this 45 degree thing other than the football, but we can, we don't have to change topics right away.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:19.560
But like the football being, having this depth effect to it actually made it like harder for me to catch the ball a lot of times.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:31.920
Especially because it's also shifting your controls in a way that I think we've complained about before, where if you're pressing up, you're actually pressing up into the, you're actually going to move up into the right.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:42.060
So it's all like cardinal, it's all cardinal directions if they put like a compass on your screen and shifted it a bit.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.480
It's not even like it's a broadcast view, you know?

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:50.500
No. This is the closest they could get to a broadcast view.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:58.920
Yeah. And yet you're still like, because of the 45 degree thing too, like a lot of the field is cut off at all times.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:09.260
Yeah. And, and I was like, okay, maybe they did this so that there would be more visibility, but like you have all your visibility in the horizontal view.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:22.980
Like that was like the problem with, with 10 yard fight and any other game that may or may not have had a vertical orientation, um, was that you need to see downfield and you couldn't see downfield.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:34.380
And this is taking like the worst of both worlds here, um, by kind of obfuscating your controls a bit and also limiting your view.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:41.440
Now, at least it has like, it, it understands that at like the, the most zoomed in points.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:52.880
So a lot of the time, uh, at least when you're passing, it will zoom out to show more of the field, but it's still very strange, uh, how, how it goes about that.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:58.240
And another parallel to 10 yard fight, uh, which I promise I'm, uh, you know, I'll get off this.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:13.200
I'm not, I'm not really saying that they're on the same level in terms of controls and depth, but it's interesting that when you start the game, uh, in 10 yard fight, if you recall, you started off being like choosing your difficulty and your difficulty was like, is this a high school football match?

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:16.320
A college football match, you know, like the pros.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:20.600
And, and that was like some nice flavor text that wasn't necessary.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:24.740
It, you weren't expecting it in that game in this one, they stripped that.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:27.700
And they're just like level one, level two, level three, level four.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:28.680
It's like, which one are you?

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:29.700
And it's like, what does that mean?

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:31.120
What does it mean to be level four?

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:39.960
Yeah. I think maybe a typical easy, medium hard would help here, but I didn't really think about that.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.080
I, that's just, that's where the parallels end though.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:48.060
Uh, at least for me, uh, then it starts to, it does, it does have a little more depth to it.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:57.400
Uh, you do have substitutions, you have injuries mid game, you have, um, the ability to, uh, fumble the ball, intercept all that fun stuff.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:03.160
So, uh, talking about the actual game now, the moment to moment, what did you think about the presentation?

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:14.700
We mentioned that this isn't quite meeting the, uh, broadcast values, but other than the fact that the field is somewhat cut off, how is the presentation of football in this game?

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:21.040
So one of the things that I appreciate about this game is that at least everything is there.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:32.680
Um, in a way that it, it, not so much in 10 yard fight, like where it was like, you just can't do the things that you should be able to do in football.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.560
Uh, that tech mobile definitely solved.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:43.340
And this one has solved in a more, uh, I would say, come not complete.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:51.600
Uh, it, it has solved this in a more comprehensive way, but not in a way that is easy to play like there.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:58.400
So the first thing I was going to say at one point while I was playing this game, I was like, Oh, I can't wait to say this.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:05.820
They call it NES play action football, but in nowhere in the, the, the playbook is there a play action pass.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:13.060
Now I found out that if I had to, I had to do a button combination to change the page of the playbook and lo and behold, there's the play action pass.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:28.660
But I was just, I was actually surprised that it was there and able to be implemented like, uh, everything in terms of the playbook, all of these different play concepts on the, on the defensive and offensive side of the ball.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:32.440
Uh, like the fact that they're there is just impressive to me.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:33.880
Like screen passes.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.040
I don't think you can even do in tech mobile.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:50.280
Um, but in terms of how it feels to play these things, it's like, it's just like the execution, the timing, the feel of controlling these, these players.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.860
It's really not hitting the mark.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:58.280
It feels very sluggish, uh, where, where a tech mobile felt very snappy.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:05.980
Um, in terms of presentation, like, like present, like a broadcast way, like it, it, it's,

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:12.000
it's more like being at a game cause you're seeing everything on the scoreboard, uh, which I guess is all right.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:22.180
Like it's like, there's at least like you see the, the ref and you see like what quote unquote highlights on, on the, uh, the jumbotron.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:26.200
